# 🎤 18. INTERVIEW QUESTION OF THE DAY

### Why is a HashMap often used to optimize an O(n²) problem?

Strong answer:

> “The brute-force solution often repeatedly searches for information inside the array, which can take O(n) per operation. A HashMap provides average O(1) lookup, allowing us to store previously processed information and avoid repeated searches. This can reduce an O(n²) solution to approximately O(n), at the cost of additional memory.”

